fihrist:manuscript_26572 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 972" ;
    dct:date "1645-08-16" ;
    dct:description """An isolated copy of the first part of the first volume of the Ḥabīb al-Siyar (Beloved of Biographies), originally completed
                     by the author Ghiyās̲ al-Dīn ibn Humām al-Dīn (ca. 1475–1535) known as Khvāndamīr (1487–1524 CE) in 937 AH (1530–31 CE) .
                     He presents a general history spanning the pre-Islamic period
                     until the reign of Shāh Ismāʿīl I, which dedicates to then-governor of
                     Herat, Karīm al-Din Khvājah Ḥabīb-Allāh
                        Sāvajī (fl. early-mid 16th c.) , hence the title. the entire work consists of a preface, an introduction, three
                     volumes—each of which contains four sections appended with lists of names of
                     prominent figures associated with each period—followed by an epilogue. This
                     volume covers This volume opens with the histories of the Persian kings after
                     the creation of Adam up to the prophet of Islam.""" ;
