fihrist:manuscript_26596 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 996" ;
    dct:date "1947-12-25" ;
    dct:description """A sole surviving carbon copy of Sunāt-i Dihkadah (Village Sonata), a musical opera in three acts composed by modern
                            Iranian poet, Dr. Majd al-Dīn Mīr
                                Fakhrā'ī (1910–1972) , pen-named Gulchīn-i
                                Gīlānī (Rose-plucker of Gilan), on Christmas, 1947 in London . He sent it together with an
                            autograph letter to Professor A. J. Arberry , 28 Dec 1947 .""" ;
