fihrist:manuscript_6731 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 246" ;
    dct:date "1676" ;
    dct:description """The volume contains complete, albeit unillustrated, copies of both the Haft Paykar (Seven Portraits) and story of Laylī and Majnūn with occasionally variant lines. 
                     Note that the colophons indicate that when restored, a bookbinder inadvertantly reversed the order in which these two works usually appear within the Khamsah .""" ;
