fihrist:manuscript_6736 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 250" ;
    dct:date "1694-12-28" ;
    dct:description """An incomplete copy of the first book of the Mas̲navī-i Ma‘navī (Spiritual Couplets) by Jalāl
                        al-Dīn Rūmī (1207–1273) . Part of a six-volume set (Rylands Persian MS 250–255) completed for the eldest son of the Mughal ruler ‘Ālamgīr I, Prince
                     Muḥammad Mu‘aẓẓam Bahādur Shāh, who would later
                     rule as Shāh ‘Ālam
                        Bahādur I (r. 1707–1712) . Two scribes named Sirāj al-Dīn ibn
                           Sayyid Bayāzīd Kūrahvī Rūdawlī and ‘Abd al-Karīm ibn Muḥammad Ḥasan completed the individual books in different locations between 1695 to 1699 CE . The former finished this volume in Calcutta (Kolkata) on 11 Jumādá I, '38th regnal year [of 
                                    ‘Ālamgīr I], (1106 AH, 28 Dec. 1694 CE) .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_6736" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial """Calcutta
                        (Kolkata)""" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_6736_person_15097572_edt,
