fihrist:manuscript_6754 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 267" ;
    dct:date "probably between 1783 and 1793 CE" ;
    dct:description """A complete, unillustrated copy of the romance of Yūsuf va
                        Zulaykhā , which comprises the fifth of seven books in the collection
                     entitled Haft Awrang (Seven Thrones), composed by Timurid-era
                     poet ‘Abd al-Raḥmān Jāmī (d. 1492) in 957 AH (1550–51 CE) . A
                     mystical love story of the Prophet
                        Joseph and Potiphar's wife Zulaykhā , the author primarily drew
                     inspiration from the twelfth chapter of the Qur'ān Sūrah Yūsuf and references by prior poets. A scribe named ‘Abd al-Raḥīm
                        Bayg probably copied this undated volume for Sir William Jones in Calcutta
                        (Kolkata) between 1783 and 1793 CE .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_6754" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Calcutta (Kolkata)" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
