fihrist:manuscript_7035 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 539" ;
    dct:date "1859-08-05" ;
    dct:description """The Dīvān-i Shams-i Tabrīzī (Dīvān of Shams of Tabriz, also known as the Dīvān-i Kabīr , of 'Large Dīvān') contains primarily ghazal lyric poems by famed medieval poet Jalāl al-Dīn Rūmī (1207–1273) named in honour of his friend, Shams Tabrizī (d. 1247) , whom he frequently invokes in place of his own pen name in the final lines. Jaykishan Dās (1832–1905) , who subsequently participated in the Aligarh educational reform movement and ultimately served as secretary then co-President of the Scientific Society, completed this large volume in Wazirabad, Punjab at the behest of Colonel George William Hamilton on 5 August 1859. 
                     The text appears to include all of the minor poems; however, many feature variant lines in comparison with critical editions. This volume also bears a delicately illuminated headpiece with similar floral decoration painted on the exterior covers.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7035" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Wazirabad, Punjab" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_7035_person_22161693743415930845_cataloguer,
