fihrist:manuscript_7120 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 619" ;
    dct:description """A selection of traditional prayers compiled by prolific Shī‘ī scholar Mullā Muḥammad Bāqir ibn Muḥammad Taqī al-Majlisi al-Isfahani (ca. 1627–1699 . 
                     Dedicated to Safavid ruler Ḥusayn I (b. 1668, r. –1726 the author describes how he excerpted this text arranged in fourteen chapters and a conclusion from his much larger four-volume collection of traditions, Biḥār al-Anvār (Oceans of Lights), as an aid for the devout.""" ;
