fihrist:manuscript_7196 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 694" ;
    dct:date "1684" ;
    dct:description "A Persian commentary by Khalīl Ibn al-Ghāzī al-Qazvīnī of Kitāb al-ṣalawāt کتاب الصلوةکتاب الصلوة the eleventh book of the great work on religious law of the Shi’ite traditions Usūl al-Kāfī اصول الكافي ، by Kulaynī, Muḥammad ibn Yaʻqūb, d. 941? كليني، محمد بن يعقوب . Al-Kāfī, writen originally in Arabic, contains some 80 thousand traditions, divided into 33 books (for the titles see Ethe, 2667, p. 1451). The present Persian commentary, a response to the royal command, as stated in the preface, was commenced in the month of Rajab the year 1070 شروع شد در شرح کتاب یازدهم است بتاریخ رجب سال هزار و هفتاد هجری , by then the commentator had already completed the first ten books of the Al-Kāfī the titles of which are given in the preface 1v کتاب العقل و کتاب التوحید و کتاب الحجه و کتاب الحجه و کتاب الایمان و الکفر و کتاب الدعا و کتاب فضل القرآن و کتاب العشرة و کتاب الجنایز and at the end of this work he states that it would be followed by Kitāb al-Zakāt این آخر کتاب الصلوة است از کتاب کافی از ابو جعفر کلینی... و در عقب آن می آید کتاب الزکوة قدوفق الشارح خلیل بن الغازی القزوینی... The Persian commentary is divided into one hundred and three bāb باب" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7196" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_7196_person_1632455_aut_Persian_MS_694_item1,
        contrib:manuscript_7196_person_56454583_cataloguer,
        contrib:manuscript_7196_person_60393215_oth,
        contrib:manuscript_7196_person_97751058_fmo,
        contrib:manuscript_7196_person_9985420_fmo,
        contrib:manuscript_7196_person_f4204_fmo,
        contrib:manuscript_7196_person_f6379_dnr,
        contrib:manuscript_7196_person_f830_fmo ;
    mdhn:hasItem item:manuscript_7196_Persian_MS_694_item1 ;
