fihrist:manuscript_7203 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 70" ;
    dct:date "1807-07-28" ;
    dct:description """A complete unillustrated copy of the romance of Yūsuf va
                        Zulaykhā , which comprises the second of seven books in the
                     collection entitled Haft Awrang (Seven Thrones) by ‘Abd al-Raḥmān Jāmī (d. 1492) , in 957 AH (1550–51 CE) . A
                     mystical love story of the Prophet
                        Joseph and Potiphar's wife, the author primarily drew inspiration
                     from the twelfth chapter of the Qur'ān Sūrah Yūsuf and
                     references by prior poets. A scribe named Muḥammad ‘Alī Khvansar completed this manuscript at
                        the start of Jumādà I 1222 AH (End of July 1807 CE) for Thomas Sydenham , British Resident at Hyderabad .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7203" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Hyderabad" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
