fihrist:manuscript_7335 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 828" ;
    dct:description """The Muqaddimah (Preface) to the Ẓafarnāmah (Book of Victory) composed by historian Sharaf al-Dīn ʻAlī Yazdī (d. 1454) in
                     822 AH (1419–1420 CE), and frequently referred to by another title, the Tārīkh-i Jahāngīr (History of the World-Seizer). He later
                     completed the entire work in 828 AH (1424–1425 CE) for the Timurid prince and
                     bibliophile, Ibrāhīm Sulṭān b. Shāh Rukh (1394–1435) to chronicle the life and
                     exploits of his patron's father Shāh Rukh Mīrzā (b. 1337, r. 1405–1447) and grandfather Tīmūr (b. 1336, r.
                        1370–1405) , founder of the Timurid dynasty (1370–1507). The
                     preface does not always appear in copies of the Ẓafarnāmah (Book
                     of Victory), but as a separate standalone work, as in this manuscript. A scribe
                     named Qā'im Muḥammad possibly completed this
                     undated volume in the in Bengal in the early 18th century CE .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_7335" ;
    dct:language "fa" ;
    dct:spatial "Bengal" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_The_University_of_Manchester_Library ;
