fihrist:manuscript_7408 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Persian MS 898" ;
    dct:date """1224
                                AH (1809–10 CE)""" ;
    dct:description """The last part of three complete volumes, bound in two (together
                            with Persian MS 897 ), of the Siyar
                                al-Mutaʼakhkhirīn (Review of Modern Times), a general
                            history of India after the death of the Mughal Emperor ‘Alamgīr I in 1707 until 1195 AH (1781 CE). The
                            author, Ghulām Husain Khān Ṭabaṭāḅāī, a son of Patna Vice-Regent Sayyid
                            ‘Alī Khān and cousin of ‘Alīvardī Khān, Nawwab of Bengal
                                (b. 1676 r. 1740–1756) , composed this text in circa 1780–1784 , and
                            dedicated it to Governor-General of Bengal, Warren Hastings . This second volume commences with the
                            ‘Ālamgīr's death in 1707 then continues until 1195 AH
                                (1781 CE).""" ;
