    rdfs:label "Persian MS 910" ;
    dct:description """A fine copy containing the Baysunghur introduction and one hundred illustrations. Completed
                     by two groups of earlier 16th century and later early 17th century Safavid
                     painters, many scenes bears signs of overpainting, which together with many
                     historical repairs, and the binding, all appear probably executed in
                     India.""" ;
